iio: adc: ad7768-1: do not force a SYNC pulse in ad7768_scan_direct()

Stable commit a12fb673b3a67 ("iio: adc: ad7768-1: fix one-shot mode data
acquisition") makes ad7768_scan_direct() switch to one-shot mode first, and
then re-init the completion and send a SYNC pulse to trigger the sample.

Downstream main already carries the newer upstream rework (c14bb04412f13 /
cbeebc5d1f94e "remove switch to one-shot mode" and "disable IRQ autoenable"),
where the ADC stays in continuous mode and the IRQ is enabled around the wait.
The conflict was resolved to the downstream scan_direct(), but the stable hunk
that follows the conflict still got merged and added a second
reinit_completion() plus an unneeded SYNC pulse, which would restart the
continuous conversion. Drop those stale lines.

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/ad7768-1.c b/drivers/iio/adc/ad7768-1.c
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/ad7768-1.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/ad7768-1.c
@@ -487,13 +487,6 @@
 	reinit_completion(&st->completion);
 	enable_irq(st->spi->irq);
 
-	reinit_completion(&st->completion);
-
-	/* One-shot mode requires a SYNC pulse to generate a new sample */
-	ret = ad7768_send_sync_pulse(st);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
 	ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&st->completion,
 					  msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
 	disable_irq(st->spi->irq);
